  "mode": "build",
  "concepts": ["backtracking"],
  "prerequisites": [],
  "story": "Guests numbered from 0 sit in a row, one chair each. Some of them have quarrelled: clash[a][b] is 1 when guests a and b must not sit side by side (and then clash[b][a] is 1 too). How many different seating orders are there? With three guests where 0 and 1 have quarrelled, only 0 2 1 and 1 2 0 work: 2 orders. seat(table, last, used) counts the ways to seat everyone still standing when guest last has just sat down; table is the clash table passed along, and used[g] is 1 for a guest already seated.",
  "io": {
    "inputs": [
      {"name": "clash", "type": "array<array<num>>"}
    ],
    "output": {"type": "num"}
  },
  "constraints": {
    "n": {"min": 1, "max": 6},
    "notes": ["There are 1 to 6 guests; clash has a row and a column for each.", "clash[a][a] is 0."]
  },
  "blocks": {
    "allow": ["arith.add", "arr.append", "arr.get", "arr.len", "arr.set", "cmp.eq", "ctrl.for_range", "ctrl.if", "ctrl.return", "fn.call3", "lit.num", "logic.and", "new.array", "var.get", "var.set"],
    "maxBlocks": 132
  },
  "limits": {"maxOps": 324650, "maxDepth": 32, "maxAlloc": 100},
  "hints": ["The program tries every guest as the first to sit: SET ELEMENT their place in a list of seated guests to 1, CALL seat, then set it back to 0.", "seat: FOR every guest g still standing, IF table[last][g] is 0, sit g down (SET ELEMENT used[g] to 1), add CALL seat(table, g, used) to the count, and stand g up again (SET ELEMENT used[g] to 0).", "Count the guests still standing as you go: IF nobody is standing, everyone is seated and that is 1 order. A guest who stays seated after their turn is missing from every later order."],
  "validators": {"output": "equal"},
